WHATNOW

What tam-edit is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-18, with W2


STATE

  tam-edit is Fred's fork of micro, rewritten in C11 so it links only
  libtam and the C library. The C11 editor lives on branch c11, pushed;
  the Go version stays on master. VERSION reads 1.0.4 (the footer shows
  it).

  All five migration milestones are complete (ROADMAP.md, 1.0.0 on
  2026-11-13): editing, views and configuration, syntax highlighting,
  search, encodings, shell, multi-cursor, the parity audit
  (docs/PARITY_AUDIT.md), fuzzing and packaging. Since then: fixes to
  arrow keys, softwrap boundaries, the softwrap goal column, the version
  in the footer, and DeleteWordLeft (W2, 61cc02c0).

  reviews/review-001.md, a review of the cursor code, found eight
  issues. #1 (softwrap goal column after Home/End/word moves, 880cbe4e)
  and #3 (act_delete_word_left multi-cursor and edit pipeline, 61cc02c0)
  are fixed.


NEXT

